 {"id": "CF-358", "title": "A cloned lane's namespace is never FK-checked, its workdir may not exist, and a re-run silently reverts hand-configured fields", "status": "pending", "priority": "P2", "complexity": "medium", "reasoning": "Measured on the same fixture: `--namespace` accepts a name that exists nowhere and leaves a dangling namespace_id with exit 0; `--workdir /nonexistent/nope` is accepted; and re-running over a row someone configured by hand silently reverts five fields (enabled 1->0, prompt_mode replace->append, prompt replaced, tasks->cooldown, 43200->21600) while printing two conflicting lines about the row already existing.", "acceptance_criteria": "1. A namespace that does not exist is a FAIL before the write.\n2. A workdir that does not exist is a FAIL (or an explicit --allow-missing-workdir).\n3. A re-run over an existing row reports each field it would change and requires --force to change it.", "created_at": "2026-11-05T20:30:54Z", "updated_at": "2026-11-05T20:30:54Z"}
 {"id": "CF-359", "title": "The bus worker's reply ladder is four requirements, not one, and the audience form cannot be produced by the shipped transcript()", "status": "pending", "priority": "P2", "complexity": "medium", "reasoning": "Measured against a real crier v0.2.0 instance with `scheduler` enrolled as a protected service identity: the shipped body fails at `sender` (403), then `idempotency_key` (400), then the audience header (401), then the signature (401) because the audience header changes the signed string. A 201 is reachable only by signing a 5-line transcript with `audience:`, and transcript() has no audience form — no configuration fixes it. Also measured: redelivery suppresses execution but re-posts the cached envelope, so one dispatch yields two queued results (queue_depth 1 -> 2), and the loop has no backoff or jitter.", "acceptance_criteria": "1. transcript() can produce the audience form, or the worker signs what crier actually requires.\n2. A redelivery does not add a second queue entry.\n3. The loop uses backoff with jitter between polls, proven by timing.", "created_at": "2026-11-05T20:30:54Z", "updated_at": "2026-11-05T20:30:54Z"}
